eive  of these interventions we're going to  want to facilitate a more  accurate conveyance of information  great thank you very much uh next  question is for stefania  um with regard to your atlasing project  uh  what what's a realistic number of driver  lines that you think  you can um analyze and archive  and what's what's the throughput of your  of your pipeline right now  uh let me make sure i understood your  question so  how many months realistically it's going  to take to  uh go through different um samples and  genotypes is that the  question how many more yeah generally  yeah i mean just generally you know how  labor intensive is it and  how how large are the data sets and you  know how he's used it to navigate  around that at the moment of prince  philip  my technician is uh working around the  clock  on this and so essentially in terms of  the pipeline  he takes probably um  one week to process the tissue and  to get his images the image more or less  and consider the age of the animals  and when they are processed because you  process them as adult  animals uh let's say everything together  uh probably two to three months  just for imaging and compiling the data  analysis  and then for  data for further data analysis we are  going to send  our samples to a  company to outsource the analysis  but uh you know we are planning to um  apply the pipeline to different mouse  genotypes  and at the moment we have a little bit  of backlog  caused by the coronavirus so for me it's  a little bit um unrealistically i can't  really  for see how long it's going to take at  the moment but normally i would say  that for  i was we were pretty fast until now  let's say in  three months we have uh gone through at  least an n of three for two different  genotypes  uh two genotypes  great thanks and hopefully you and  everybody else will soon be able to get  back to work  and do so safely um the next question  uh yes the next question uh  it was not tagged to a specific spea